abstract: >
  Experimental code for ExSASCA, a fast and exact probabilistic inference method for
  soft analytical side-channel attacks (SASCA) on the Advanced Encryption Standard (AES),
  based on knowledge compilation and tractable probabilistic circuits. The repository
  contains the CNF encoding and SDD compilation pipeline for the AES MixColumns
  operation, the ExSASCA inference implementation, and the scripts reproducing the
  experiments of the accompanying ICML 2024 paper. Developed with funding from the NEO
  project (Next Generation Molecular Data Storage), Horizon Europe / EIC Pathfinder
  Challenges grant agreement No 101115317.

